The `qr_numregions` field originates from a DLM_QUERY_REGION network message and is used directly as the loop bound without any validation against `O2NM_MAX_REGIONS` (32). Since the `qr_regions` buffer is allocated to hold at most 32 entries, a crafted message can set `qr_numregions` to a value up to 255, causing the loops to read beyond the buffer and trigger an out-of-bounds read.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
if (qr->qr_numregions > O2NM_MAX_REGIONS) {
