Reason:
This bounds check is added before any loops that iterate over `qr_numregions`. If the received value exceeds the maximum allowed (O2NM_MAX_REGIONS), the function immediately returns an error, preventing the out-of-bounds read. The check ensures that only valid region counts are processed. (Note: This patch does not fix the separate off-by-one error in the inner loop with `<=`; that is addressed by a subsequent patch.)

